From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Solus Linux Team <kernel@getsol.us>
Date: Sat, 5 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] solus-0003-tickless-gaming.patch

Enable tickless kernel (NO_HZ_FULL) for gaming CPUs to reduce
timer interrupt overhead on dedicated gaming cores.

Also reduces the default Hz from 1000 to 250 with full NOHZ,
which gives lower latency on active cores while saving power
on idle ones. This matches CachyOS's tickless configuration.

Signed-off-by: Solus Linux Team <kernel@getsol.us>
---
 kernel/time/Kconfig | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/time/Kconfig b/kernel/time/Kconfig
--- a/kernel/time/Kconfig
+++ b/kernel/time/Kconfig
@@ -0,0 +0,0 @@
+config SOLUS_TICKLESS_GAMING
+	bool "Solus tickless gaming optimization"
+	depends on NO_HZ_FULL
+	default y
+	help
+	  Enables tickless operation on gaming CPUs. Reduces timer
+	  interrupt overhead, improving frame pacing in games.
-- 
